{
	title: 'A session stays on its account until it is limited',
	spec: 'Least-used rotation (task 61) picks an account only when a session has none yet or its account is limited, broken or out of quota; otherwise every turn stays on the account the session used last, as the old Hal did, so the prompt cache (which is per account) survives. Re-picking every turn would flip between evenly used accounts, because the one just used is then the busier one. The choice is kept per session in memory; a restart may pick again. Tests: two evenly used accounts, several turns in a row use the same one; a 429 on it moves the session to the least used other.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Task 61 had re-picked on each turn's first round (ProviderRequest.newTurn from turns.ts); that flag is gone. auth.order moves the session's chosen account (auth.state.chosen, key '<kind> <session>') to the front; pick() still skips it when limited (limits.ason) or broken, and records whichever account it returns, so after a 429 the session sticks to the new one. Out-of-quota answers are 429s (provider.ts classifies every 429 as limited), so they rotate the same way."
	],
	needs: ['61'],
	foldInto: ['61']
}
